# --- Nano CC Tooltip ---
machine.computingcenter.machinetype=Nano Computing Center
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.desc=§7A computing center: racks turn computation components into computation, or spend it on research and scanning.
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.flavour=§7The faster it computes, the faster your meter spins.
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.modes.header=§6Modes:
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.modes.computing=§7· Mode §b0§7 §bNano Computing§7: racks produce computation, emitted through a data output hatch or the wireless network
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.modes.research=§7· Mode §b1§7 §bResearch Station§7: spends computation on Assembly Line research, needs an Object Holder and a data stick
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.modes.scanner=§7· Mode §b2§7 §bScanner§7: scans items or fluids and produces scanner results
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.modes.switch=§7· Screwdriver cycles the modes; §cblocked while running or while heat remains
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.heat.header=§6Heat:
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.heat.limit=§7· Heat ceiling §b10,000,000§7; above it every component in the racks §cmelts§7 and the machine shuts down
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.heat.cooling=§7· Idle cooling removes §bmax(heat/1000, 100)§7 per second; every §b10,000§7 heat can be removed for §b100,000L§7 of Gelid Cryotheum, also while running
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.heat.lock=§7· While heat remains the racks stay §clocked§7 and overclock §ccannot be disabled§7
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.power.header=§6Power:
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.power.computing=§7· Nano Computing: §b1A§7 §eUEV§7 base plus §b1A§7 §eUEV§7 per full §b100,000§7 computation (rounded up)
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.power.research=§7· Research Station: §brecipe EU/t + produced computation / 2§7 (rack and external computation both count)
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.power.scanner=§7· Scanner: the larger of the recipe EU/t and the §eUV§7 recipe voltage
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.power.overclock=§7· Overclock (Nano Computing only, GUI toggle): ratios §b1..100§7, heat builds up only while it is on
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.details=§dDetails:§7 computation fed in from outside is forwarded directly and does not add to the Nano Computing power surcharge
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.details.hint=§7· Mode §b0§7 needs racks and a data output hatch; modes §b1/2§7 need an Object Holder and an output bus; every mode needs an energy hatch
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.details.hatch=§7· Wireless output is toggled with a wire cutter in Nano Computing; a Wireless Computation Output hatch also satisfies the data output hatch
machine.computingcenter.tooltip.6=§7No maintain hatch require!

