machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.desc=§7Space Elevator module: mines ores from the asteroid band at the set distance
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.flavour=§7F U C C
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.structure.header=§6Structure:
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.structure.rail=§7· Must be mounted on a §eSpace Elevator§7 with a §eSpace Elevator Motor MK-V§7 or better; §cstops without a connected elevator
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.structure.frame=§7· Single-block controller at the §e4th layer, front centre§7; the skeleton is §eSpace Elevator Base Casing§7
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.structure.hatches=§7· Needs §b1§7 Input Hatch, §b1§7 Input Bus and §b1§7 Output Bus; the §eData Access Hatch§7 may sit on the module or on the elevator
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.mining.header=§6Mining:
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.mining.distance=§7· Distance (§b0-300§7) picks the pool: only asteroid recipes whose distance range contains the set value are used; with cycle on the distance sweeps §bset value ± range§7 by the step size
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.mining.asteroid=§7· Each operation draws one asteroid by weight, then rolls its ores by weight and chance
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.mining.size=§7· Each parallel always yields the asteroid's §bminimum§7 and can reach up to its §bmaximum§7 through an §abonus chance§7; higher plasma tiers mean higher chance and faster mining, higher overdrive means faster mining but a §clower§7 chance (capped at §b75%§7)
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.mining.plasma=§7· Every parallel uses §b825L§7 §eHelium Plasma§7 / §b550L§7 §eBismuth Plasma§7 / §b375L§7 §eRadon Plasma§7 / §b250L§7 §eTechnetium Plasma§7 / §b150L§7 §ePlutonium-241 Plasma§7, picks the highest tier available and rounds the total up
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.mining.supplies=§7· Uses matching-tier §eMining Drones§7, §eDrills§7 and matching rod parts; a drone may also sit in the controller slot
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.power.header=§6Power & Parallel:
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.power.wireless=§7· Draws power from the §eWireless Network§7: §e1A MAX§7 base, §e1A UXV§7 per extra parallel
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.power.parallel=§7· Parallel is capped at §b2,147,483,647§7 (integer limit) and further limited by §ecomputation§7, §eplasma§7 and the input stock
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.power.crossrecipe=§7· Each main batch runs up to §b64§7 independent mining recipes back to back (cross-recipe parallel), §b1§7 tick per recipe
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.power.computation=§7· Each operation consumes §bastroid computation × actual parallels§7, drawn from a §eData Access Hatch§7; a finished §eAsteroid Outpost§7 lowers computation and plasma costs
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.details=§dDetails:§7 the parameter panel sets distance (§b0-300§7), overdrive (§b100-200§7), cycle (§b0/1§7), range (§b0-150§7), step (§b0-20§7) and whitelist (§b0/1§7), plus the ore filter
machine.spacemoduleminer.tooltip.details.hint=§7· With the whitelist on only filtered ores are mined; with it off the filter §cexcludes§7 them; the filter holds §b64§7 slots
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.desc=§7A space pump module: pick a planet and a gas in each recipe slot and pipe the fluid into an output hatch
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.flavour=§7Succ. This machine sucks planets dry and drains your wireless network
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.structure.header=§6Structure:
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.structure.elevator=§7· Needs a §9Space Elevator§7 carrying the §9Space Elevator Acceleration Rail MK-V§7, or the module will not start
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.structure.module=§7· A single-block controller with a skeletal structure, built from §bSpace Elevator Base Casing§7 and connected to the Space Elevator
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.structure.hatch=§7· Fluid leaves through an §bOutput Hatch§7; at least one is required
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.selection.header=§6Recipe selection:
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.selection.slots=§7· The controller holds §b4§7 independent recipes, each with its own planet type, gas type and parallel count
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.selection.rules=§7· The planet and gas type pick the pumped fluid; a slot with no matching entry stays idle
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.selection.batch=§7· Batch size §b1..128§7; a main run takes §b20§7 ticks times the batch, and one output caps at §b2,147,483,647§7 (integer limit)
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.power.header=§6Power:
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.power.base=§7· Draws power directly from the wireless network, no energy hatch needed; base cost §b1A MAX§7, each extra parallel adds §b1A UXV§7
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.power.parallel=§7· Parallel caps at §b1,000,000§7 and power scales linearly with it; the whole cost is deducted from the network when the batch starts
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.power.wireless=§7· Wireless mode only; it never draws from energy hatches, so there is no hatch-powered fallback
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.details=§dDetails:
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.details.slots=§7· The 4 slots run independently and do not block each other
machine.spacemodulepump.tooltip.details.output=§7· Output hatches need free capacity; a full hatch pauses only its own slot
