machine.nanoscale.tooltip.flavour=§7Eleven processes share one hall - the only worry is plugging the programming circuit into the wrong slot
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.selection.header=§6Mode selection:
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.selection.multimode=§7· Mode 0 (Multithreaded, default): Each input bus matches recipe pools based on the circuit it has selected; multiple pools can run in parallel and independently; input buses without a programmed circuit will not participate in recipe checking.
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.selection.pool=§7· Mode 1 (one-step circuit pool, needs the Astral Array unlock): every thread stops and the machine's main thread runs, with the pool picked by a circuit §b1..6§7 in an input bus circuit slot
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.selection.modes1=§7· Circuit §b1§7 Conversion / §b2§7 Assembly Matrix / §b3§7 SMD Processor / §b4§7 Board Processor / §b5§7 Etching Array / §b6§7 Cutting Chamber
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.selection.modes2=§7· Circuit §b7§7 Wire Tracer / §b8§7 Superconductor Splitter / §b9§7 Optical Organizer / §b10§7 Encasement Wrapper / §b11§7 Biological Coordinator
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.special.header=§6Special pool mechanics:
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.special.conversion=§7· Conversion unwraps physical packets back into real §bGT§7 items
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.special.board=§7· Board Processor keeps §b5§7 independent §b1,000,000L§7 immersion tanks, one per fluid type
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.special.optical=§7· Optical Organizer needs two different purified waters while running
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.special.etching=§7· Etching Array uses the energy hatch tier/amperage as its laser source
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.astral.header=§6Astral Array:
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.astral.enable=§7· An Astral Array in an input bus unlocks §bmode 1§7 (the machine stays in mode 0 by default); switch with a screwdriver or the GUI mode button
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.astral.mode1=§7· Mode 1 circuits: §b1§7 Processor / §b2§7 Assembly / §b3§7 Supercomputer / §b4§7 Mainframe / §b5§7 the original circuit ladder / §b6§7 the special Pico/Quantum/Planck chains
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.astral.restrict=§7· The mode cannot be switched while the machine is active (switch it off or wait until it is idle); entering mode 1 drops the threads' unfinished tasks, and the Astral Array cannot be taken out while mode 1 is running
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.astral.wirecutter=§7· A wire cutter ejects the stored Astral Array into an output bus
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.details=§dDetails:§7 mode 0 polls its inputs every §b20§7 ticks; pools settle independently and ME input buses support circuit pooling too
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.details.hint=§7· The unlocked Astral Array is saved to the item NBT: pick the machine up and place it down again, mode 1 needs no second Astral Array
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.3=§eStructure: 32 x 64 x 32, controller on the middle of the front face
machine.nanoscale.tooltip.astral=Contains an Astral Array Fabricator. Use a wire cutter to remove it.
